IMPORT prelude

-- Registration of Deeds Act 1988 (Singapore) -- what is registered, who presents it, how execution
-- is proved, and the conditions on which registration becomes complete: ss 2, 4 to 7 and 9 to 13.
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation in force from 1 October 2025, as deposited
-- at ../../registers/source-bundle/RDA1988.txt. (The deposited arrangement of sections numbers "Short
-- title" as s 2 and so runs one ahead of the body, which numbers it s 1; this encoding follows the body.)
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. A citation count across the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository found 37
-- Acts that cite the Registration of Deeds Act 1988, for an Act of only 66,000 characters (about half
-- of that legislative history). It is the deeds-registration system for land that is NOT registered
-- under the Land Titles Act 1993, and so is the other half of the picture the `land-titles-act-1993`
-- row of this repository draws for registered land.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no
-- coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: s 3 (appointment of the Registrar), s 29 (rules: none retrieved), and the legislative
-- history. No rules under the Act were retrieved, and several provisions are expressed to depend on them.

§ `Registration of Deeds Act 1988 -- registration`

§§ `2 -- the terms the Act is built from`

-- s 2(1): "'lease' INCLUDES AN AGREEMENT FOR A LEASE". "'mortgage' includes any charge on any land for
-- securing money or money's worth and any transfer of a mortgage". "'prior mortgage' includes a prior
-- charge or assignment which has been either secured by a mortgage OR PROTECTED BY A CAVEAT lodged with
-- and accepted by the Registrar as being in order for registration". "'caveator' means (a) a person who has
-- been given an estate or interest in any land by the proprietor of the land; or (b) a person who CLAIMS an
-- estate or interest". "'land' means (a) the surface of any defined parcel of the earth, so much of the
-- subterranean space below and the column of airspace above ... as is reasonably necessary for the use and
-- enjoyment of the proprietor, and includes any estate or interest therein and all vegetation growing
-- thereon and structures affixed thereto; or (b) any parcel of airspace or subterranean space held apart
-- ... described with certainty by reference to a plan approved by the Chief Surveyor".
--
-- Two consequences are used below. An AGREEMENT for a lease is a lease for the purposes of s 25. And a
-- prior charge protected only by a CAVEAT counts as a "prior mortgage" for the right to tack in s 15.

§§ `4 -- the penalty for not registering`

-- s 4: "all assurances executed or made, and all probates and letters of administration granted, before or
-- after 30 November 1988 by which any land within Singapore is affected and which have not been registered
-- under any repealed enactment, may be registered ..., and UNLESS SO REGISTERED IS NOT ADMISSIBLE IN ANY
-- COURT AS EVIDENCE OF TITLE to the land."
--
-- The sanction is evidential. An unregistered assurance is not void, and the Act does not say that it
-- passes no estate; it says a court will not admit it as evidence of title. Registration is optional in
-- form and compulsory in effect. The Act is silent on land already registered under the Land Titles Act
-- 1993, which has its own register; that is taken as a fact supplied here.
DECLARE AssuranceFacts HAS
    `affects land within Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the land is registered land under the Land Titles Act 1993` IS A BOOLEAN
    `was registered under this Act or a repealed enactment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is excluded from the Act by section 25 as a short lease with possession` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the assurance` IS AN AssuranceFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the assurance is within this Act` IF
        `the assurance`'s `affects land within Singapore`
    AND NOT `the assurance`'s `the land is registered land under the Land Titles Act 1993`
    AND NOT `the assurance`'s `is excluded from the Act by section 25 as a short lease with possession`

GIVEN `the assurance` IS AN AssuranceFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a court will admit the assurance as evidence of title` IF
        NOT `the assurance is within this Act` `the assurance`
    OR  `the assurance`'s `was registered under this Act or a repealed enactment`

GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an unregistered assurance is void` IF
    FALSE

§§ `5 -- what must be presented`

-- s 5(1): a person desiring to register an instrument must present --
--   (a) for instruments other than private Acts, probates, letters of administration, orders of court and
--       certificates of appointment of a trustee in bankruptcy: THE ORIGINAL AND A MEMORIAL;
--   (b) for orders of court and certificates of appointment: AN OFFICE COPY AND A MEMORIAL;
--   (c) for a private Act: a copy purporting to be printed or published by the Government Printer and a
--       memorial;
--   (d) for probates or letters of administration: a memorial prepared in accordance with the rules
--       TOGETHER WITH THE PROBATE OR LETTERS themselves; and
--   (e) for a memorandum of lien or charge, or of discharge: the original and a memorial.
DECLARE InstrumentKind IS ONE OF
    `an ordinary assurance`
    `a private Act`
    `a probate or letters of administration`
    `an order of court`
    `a certificate of appointment of a trustee in bankruptcy`
    `a memorandum of lien or charge, or of discharge`

DECLARE Presented HAS
    `the original` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an office copy` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a copy printed or published by the Government Printer` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the probate or letters of administration themselves` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a memorial` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the kind` IS AN InstrumentKind, `what was presented` IS A Presented
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `what was presented meets section 5(1)` IF
        `what was presented`'s `a memorial`
    AND CONSIDER `the kind`
        WHEN `an ordinary assurance` THEN `what was presented`'s `the original`
        WHEN `a memorandum of lien or charge, or of discharge` THEN `what was presented`'s `the original`
        WHEN `an order of court` THEN `what was presented`'s `an office copy`
        WHEN `a certificate of appointment of a trustee in bankruptcy` THEN `what was presented`'s `an office copy`
        WHEN `a private Act` THEN `what was presented`'s `a copy printed or published by the Government Printer`
        WHEN `a probate or letters of administration` THEN `what was presented`'s `the probate or letters of administration themselves`

-- s 5(2) and (4): on acceptance for PROVISIONAL registration the Registrar allots a volume and number and
-- endorses the date and time. If the land "has not been surveyed and demarcated to the satisfaction of the
-- Chief Surveyor", the person presenting "is deemed to have made an application for the land to be
-- surveyed and demarcated".
GIVEN `the land has been surveyed and demarcated to the satisfaction of the Chief Surveyor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the presenter is deemed to have applied for a survey` IF
    NOT `the land has been surveyed and demarcated to the satisfaction of the Chief Surveyor`

§§ `6 -- a lien or charge that is not registered`

-- s 6(1): where a lien or charge is claimed "in respect of any UNPAID PURCHASE MONEY or by reason of any
-- DEPOSIT OF TITLE DEEDS or otherwise", a memorandum signed by the person against whom it is claimed may be
-- provisionally registered on presentation by any person claiming to be interested.
-- s 6(2): "No such lien or charge has ANY EFFECT OR PRIORITY as against any assurance for VALUABLE
-- CONSIDERATION until a memorandum thereof has been registered in accordance with this Act."
-- s 6(3): when satisfied, any person claiming an interest may register a memorandum of discharge.
--
-- So the unpaid vendor's lien and the equitable mortgage by deposit of title deeds, both of which exist
-- without registration at common law, are worth nothing against a later purchaser or mortgagee for value
-- until a signed memorandum is registered. The memorandum must be signed by the person against whom the
-- charge is claimed, so a lienee who will not sign leaves the unpaid vendor needing a caveat instead.
DECLARE LienFacts HAS
    `a lien or charge is claimed for unpaid purchase money, by deposit of title deeds, or otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a memorandum signed by the person against whom it is claimed has been registered` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the competing assurance is for valuable consideration` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the competing assurance was registered before the memorandum` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the lien` IS A LienFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the lien or charge has effect against the competing assurance` IF
        `the lien`'s `a lien or charge is claimed for unpaid purchase money, by deposit of title deeds, or otherwise`
    AND (    NOT `the lien`'s `the competing assurance is for valuable consideration`
         OR  (    `the lien`'s `a memorandum signed by the person against whom it is claimed has been registered`
              AND NOT `the lien`'s `the competing assurance was registered before the memorandum`))

§§ `7 -- provisional registration becomes complete, or becomes void`

-- s 7(1): "Immediately on compliance with section 13(1) or the provisions of section 13(1), other than
-- paragraph (c) in the event of that paragraph being dispensed with, any instrument provisionally registered
-- is deemed to have been registered ..., and the date, hour and minute entered under [s 5(2)] is deemed for
-- ALL PURPOSES to be the date and time of registration."
-- s 7(4): "If at the expiration of 6 MONTHS from the date of provisional registration of any instrument
-- section 13(1) (OTHER THAN PARAGRAPH (c)) has not been fully complied with, then the provisional
-- registration is VOID for all purposes and all entries in respect thereof must be cancelled."
-- s 7(5): subsection (1) "does not apply to any assurance in respect of any estate or interest in any
-- RESIDENTIAL PROPERTY within the meaning of the Residential Property Act 1976".
--
-- THE SURVEY CONDITION FALLS BETWEEN THE TWO. s 7(1) needs all of s 13(1) (the survey condition (c) included,
-- unless dispensed) before registration is complete. s 7(4) voids a provisional registration only for want
-- of s 13(1) OTHER than (c). So an instrument that meets (a), (b), (d) and (e) but not the survey condition
-- (c), with no dispensation, is not complete and is not void. It stays provisionally registered
-- indefinitely. The Act does not say what its priority is in that state.
--
-- And for RESIDENTIAL PROPERTY s 7(1) is disapplied entirely, so the retrospection to the provisional date
-- is lost. The Act does not say what date applies instead.
DECLARE Conditions HAS
    `duly stamped` IS A BOOLEAN
    `arrears of land revenue remain due after demand` IS A BOOLEAN
    `boundaries surveyed and demarcated to the Chief Surveyor's satisfaction, or an endorsed assurance plan annexed` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Registrar has dispensed with the survey condition under the rules` IS A BOOLEAN
    `fees demanded remain unpaid` IS A BOOLEAN
    `in accordance with any written law applying to assurances of land not subject to the Land Titles Act` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 13(1)(a), (b), (d) and (e), which s 7(4) counts.
GIVEN `the conditions` IS A Conditions
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `conditions (a), (b), (d) and (e) of section 13(1) are met` IF
        `the conditions`'s `duly stamped`
    AND NOT `the conditions`'s `arrears of land revenue remain due after demand`
    AND NOT `the conditions`'s `fees demanded remain unpaid`
    AND `the conditions`'s `in accordance with any written law applying to assurances of land not subject to the Land Titles Act`

-- s 13(1)(c), or its dispensation under s 13(2).
GIVEN `the conditions` IS A Conditions
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the survey condition is met or dispensed with` IF
        `the conditions`'s `boundaries surveyed and demarcated to the Chief Surveyor's satisfaction, or an endorsed assurance plan annexed`
    OR  `the conditions`'s `the Registrar has dispensed with the survey condition under the rules`

GIVEN `the conditions` IS A Conditions
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the instrument may be registered under section 13` IF
        `conditions (a), (b), (d) and (e) of section 13(1) are met` `the conditions`
    AND `the survey condition is met or dispensed with` `the conditions`

DECLARE ProvisionalRegistration HAS
    `the conditions` IS A Conditions
    `months since provisional registration` IS A NUMBER
    `the assurance concerns residential property within the Residential Property Act 1976` IS A BOOLEAN

-- Complete, with retrospection to the provisional date, under s 7(1).
GIVEN `the registration` IS A ProvisionalRegistration
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the registration is complete with effect from the provisional date` IF
        `the instrument may be registered under section 13` (`the registration`'s `the conditions`)
    AND NOT `the registration`'s `the assurance concerns residential property within the Residential Property Act 1976`

-- Void, under s 7(4): six months have run and conditions other than the survey have not all been met.
GIVEN `the registration` IS A ProvisionalRegistration
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the provisional registration is void` IF
        `the registration`'s `months since provisional registration` AT LEAST 6
    AND NOT `conditions (a), (b), (d) and (e) of section 13(1) are met` (`the registration`'s `the conditions`)

-- The gap: not complete, not void.
GIVEN `the registration` IS A ProvisionalRegistration
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the instrument remains provisionally registered indefinitely` IF
        NOT `the provisional registration is void` `the registration`
    AND NOT `the registration is complete with effect from the provisional date` `the registration`
    AND `conditions (a), (b), (d) and (e) of section 13(1) are met` (`the registration`'s `the conditions`)
    AND NOT `the survey condition is met or dispensed with` (`the registration`'s `the conditions`)

-- For residential property the Act states no date of registration at all.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Act says what date of registration applies to residential property` IF
    FALSE

§§ `9, 10 -- who may present`

-- s 9(1): an assurance or caveat must not be provisionally registered unless presented by "(a) a person who
-- has executed or claims under it; (b) the legal personal representative of that person; (c) the AGENT of that
-- person or representative duly authorised by power of attorney ...; or (d) the SOLICITOR of that person or
-- that person's representative."
-- s 9(2): for a corporation or company, "(a) in the case of a corporation sole, by the corporation and in the
-- case of a company or other corporation aggregate, by a DIRECTOR OR SECRETARY; (b) by the agent ... duly
-- authorised by a power of attorney; or (c) by the solicitor of the corporation or company."
-- s 10: where executed by an agent under a power of attorney, the Registrar MAY require the power to be
-- deposited in the Registry of the Supreme Court before provisional registration.
DECLARE Presenter IS ONE OF
    `a person who executed the instrument or claims under it`
    `that person's legal personal representative`
    `their agent under a power of attorney`
    `their solicitor`
    `a director of the company`
    `the secretary of the company`
    `the corporation sole itself`
    `a stranger with no connection to it`

DECLARE PresentingFor IS ONE OF
    `an individual`
    `a corporation sole`
    `a company or other corporation aggregate`

GIVEN `the presenter` IS A Presenter, `on behalf of` IS A PresentingFor
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the presenter may present the instrument` IF
    CONSIDER `on behalf of`
    WHEN `an individual`
        THEN CONSIDER `the presenter`
             WHEN `a person who executed the instrument or claims under it` THEN TRUE
             WHEN `that person's legal personal representative` THEN TRUE
             WHEN `their agent under a power of attorney` THEN TRUE
             WHEN `their solicitor` THEN TRUE
             OTHERWISE FALSE
    WHEN `a corporation sole`
        THEN CONSIDER `the presenter`
             WHEN `the corporation sole itself` THEN TRUE
             WHEN `their agent under a power of attorney` THEN TRUE
             WHEN `their solicitor` THEN TRUE
             OTHERWISE FALSE
    WHEN `a company or other corporation aggregate`
        THEN CONSIDER `the presenter`
             WHEN `a director of the company` THEN TRUE
             WHEN `the secretary of the company` THEN TRUE
             WHEN `their agent under a power of attorney` THEN TRUE
             WHEN `their solicitor` THEN TRUE
             OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the Registrar requires the power of attorney to be deposited` IS A BOOLEAN, `it has been deposited` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a power of attorney blocks provisional registration` IF
        `the Registrar requires the power of attorney to be deposited`
    AND NOT `it has been deposited`

§§ `11, 12 -- proving that the instrument was executed`

-- s 11(1): an assurance or caveat must not be provisionally registered unless the persons who executed it,
-- their legal personal representatives, or their agents, "appear ... before the Registrar and ADMIT such
-- execution".
-- s 11(2): the Registrar must inquire whether it was executed by those who purport to have executed it,
-- satisfy himself or herself as to their identity, and as to the right of any representative or agent to appear.
-- s 11(3): if all executants appear and are known or otherwise satisfy the Registrar, and admit execution (or
-- the agent does, or the personal representative of a deceased one does), "the Registrar MUST provisionally
-- register the instrument".
-- s 11(5): the section "does not apply in the case of a person whose execution of the instrument is CERTIFIED
-- in the prescribed form ... by -- (a) an advocate and solicitor of the Supreme Court; (b) a consular officer
-- or representative of Singapore; or (c) a notary public practising in the country where the execution takes
-- place."
-- s 11(6): nor to an instrument executed by a company under its common seal, if a director or the secretary
-- appears and admits it was executed in accordance with the articles and the seal is the company's, OR the
-- execution is certified as in (5).
-- s 11(7): where there is NO NOTARY PUBLIC practising in the country, the section does not apply if an
-- advocate and solicitor certifies (a) the person executing is his or her client, (b) of full age and legal
-- capacity, and (c) he or she is satisfied the client executed it.
-- s 11(8): the same for a company executing under its common seal in such a country.
-- s 11(9): the section does not apply to an instrument executed by the Public Trustee or the Official Assignee
-- under his or her official seal.
--
-- In practice the appearance requirement is the exception. A certificate by an advocate and solicitor, a
-- consular officer or a local notary replaces it, and the s 11(7) route needs the advocate and solicitor to
-- be the executant's own lawyer.
DECLARE ExecutionProof HAS
    `all executants, or their personal representatives or agents, appeared and admitted execution` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Registrar is satisfied as to identity and the right of any representative or agent to appear` IS A BOOLEAN
    `execution was certified in the prescribed form by an advocate and solicitor, a consular officer or a local notary public` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it was executed by a company under its common seal` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a director or the secretary appeared and admitted it was executed in accordance with the articles and the seal is the company's` IS A BOOLEAN
    `there is no notary public practising in the country of execution` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an advocate and solicitor certified the signatory is the client, of full age and capacity, and that the client executed it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an advocate and solicitor certified the company is the client and executed it in accordance with its articles under its seal` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it was executed by the Public Trustee or the Official Assignee under the official seal` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the proof` IS AN ExecutionProof
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 11 is satisfied` IF
        (    `the proof`'s `all executants, or their personal representatives or agents, appeared and admitted execution`
         AND `the proof`'s `the Registrar is satisfied as to identity and the right of any representative or agent to appear`)
    OR  `the proof`'s `execution was certified in the prescribed form by an advocate and solicitor, a consular officer or a local notary public`
    OR  (    `the proof`'s `it was executed by a company under its common seal`
         AND `the proof`'s `a director or the secretary appeared and admitted it was executed in accordance with the articles and the seal is the company's`)
    OR  (    `the proof`'s `there is no notary public practising in the country of execution`
         AND `the proof`'s `an advocate and solicitor certified the signatory is the client, of full age and capacity, and that the client executed it`)
    OR  (    `the proof`'s `it was executed by a company under its common seal`
         AND `the proof`'s `there is no notary public practising in the country of execution`
         AND `the proof`'s `an advocate and solicitor certified the company is the client and executed it in accordance with its articles under its seal`)
    OR  `the proof`'s `it was executed by the Public Trustee or the Official Assignee under the official seal`

-- s 12(2): a person "who by reason of bodily infirmity is unable without risk or serious inconvenience to appear
-- at the Registry and a person IN JAIL under civil or criminal process" need not appear; the Registrar must go
-- to the house or the jail to examine them, or issue a commission.
GIVEN `unable to appear by reason of bodily infirmity without risk or serious inconvenience` IS A BOOLEAN, `in jail under civil or criminal process` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is excused from appearing at the Registry` IF
        `unable to appear by reason of bodily infirmity without risk or serious inconvenience`
    OR  `in jail under civil or criminal process`

§§ `13 -- conditions precedent to registration`

-- s 13(1): "An instrument or memorial must not be registered -- (a) unless it is duly STAMPED; (b) so long as any
-- ARREARS OF LAND REVENUE after demand for payment has been made remain due to the State in respect of the land
-- ...; (c) unless the BOUNDARIES of all lands affected ... have been SURVEYED AND DEMARCATED to the satisfaction of
-- the Chief Surveyor or unless there is annexed ... an ASSURANCE PLAN ... endorsed by the Chief Surveyor ... with
-- the caution as to the inconclusiveness of its boundaries and dimensions; (d) if the FEES for registration having
-- been demanded remain unpaid; and (e) which is not in accordance with any written law which applies to assurances
-- affecting land not subject to the Land Titles Act."
-- s 13(2): where (c) has not been complied with, the instrument may be registered "if the Registrar has granted
-- dispensation from compliance ... pursuant to the rules".
--
-- The conditions are encoded above with s 7 (`the instrument may be registered under section 13`). The land
-- revenue condition is triggered by a DEMAND having been made and arrears remaining after it: arrears that have not
-- been demanded do not block registration.
GIVEN `arrears of land revenue exist` IS A BOOLEAN, `demand for payment has been made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `land revenue arrears block registration` IF
        `arrears of land revenue exist`
    AND `demand for payment has been made`

-- s 13(3): "If by error any instrument has a wrong town subdivision or mukim number, demarcation lot number or part
-- number, or a wrong area endorsed upon it, the Collector of Land Revenue may visit the land and there hold an
-- inquiry ..., and if the Collector is satisfied that ALL THE PARTIES to the instrument WHO CAN BE FOUND WITHIN
-- SINGAPORE or their representatives (if any) admit the error and that the instrument has in fact been wrongly
-- endorsed, then, DESPITE THE ABSENCE OF ANY PARTIES WHO ARE DEAD OR HAVE LEFT SINGAPORE, the Collector may, by
-- order in writing, direct the endorsement on the instrument to be corrected".
-- s 13(5): on service of the order on the Registrar, the register and index are construed as if the corrections had
-- been in the instrument from the start.
DECLARE CorrectionFacts HAS
    `the endorsement has a wrong town subdivision, mukim, lot, part number or area` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Collector held an inquiry on the land` IS A BOOLEAN
    `all parties who can be found within Singapore, or their representatives, admit the error` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the instrument has in fact been wrongly endorsed` IS A BOOLEAN
    `some parties are dead or have left Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the correction` IS A CorrectionFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Collector may order the endorsement corrected` IF
        `the correction`'s `the endorsement has a wrong town subdivision, mukim, lot, part number or area`
    AND `the correction`'s `the Collector held an inquiry on the land`
    AND `the correction`'s `all parties who can be found within Singapore, or their representatives, admit the error`
    AND `the correction`'s `the instrument has in fact been wrongly endorsed`

-- The absence of dead or departed parties does not prevent it.
GIVEN `the correction` IS A CorrectionFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the absence of dead or departed parties prevents the correction` IF
    FALSE
